  "notes": "The parameter the research is loudest about is a mix decision: \"drums louder and drier than the Bad Boy era\". That is authored as raised `velocityTiers`, one perc lane instead of three, and a very low ghost probability — not as a different pattern, because the pattern is the same kick-1/3.5 and hard-2&4 grammar. Above that, minor soul loops with genuine motion (i–iv and i–VI–III–VII) and one major gospel family at low weight for the message records. ⚠ The sustained sub the research names is `mirror_kick` with `followRootsProb` 0.93 — \"simple root motion\" is exactly what that produces, and the engine's held-note bass rhythm saturates. ⚠ `medium`, and the inferred parameters are the drum numbers: the research says outright that this entry's parameters are inherited from its producers rather than measured from the records, so hat density, ghost placement and swing amount are the Premier/Alchemist-adjacent norm rather than a reading of Jadakiss specifically.",
